# Toolbar

Grouped controls with roving focus: one tab stop, arrows travel, inputs keep caret keys.

<div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border bg-card p-6 text-card-foreground">
	<Toolbar.Root>
		<div class="flex items-center gap-1">
			<Toolbar.Button
				class="rounded-md px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-accent"
				onclick={() => (saved += 1)}
			>
				Save
			</Toolbar.Button>
			<Toolbar.Button class="rounded-md px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-accent" disabled>
				Cut
			</Toolbar.Button>
			<Toolbar.Separator class="mx-1 h-5 border-l" />
			<Toolbar.Link href="https://example.com" class="rounded-md px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-accent">
				Help
			</Toolbar.Link>
			<Toolbar.Input aria-label="Search" placeholder="Search" class="h-9 rounded-md border bg-transparent px-3 text-sm" />
		</div>
	</Toolbar.Root>
	<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Saved: {saved} (Tab in once, arrows travel — Cut is skipped)</p>
</div>

## Anatomy

<CodeBlock code={anatomy} filename="App.svelte" />

## API reference

### Toolbar.Root

<ApiTable props={rootProps} />

`Toolbar.Button`, `Toolbar.Link`, and `Toolbar.Input` register for roving; `Group` clusters controls; `Separator` divides without ever taking focus. Buttons and links share one tab stop; the input stays tabbable with native caret keys.

## Keyboard interactions

- <Kbd>←</Kbd><Kbd>→</Kbd> move focus between controls (vertical orientation: <Kbd>↑</Kbd><Kbd>↓</Kbd>); <Kbd>Home</Kbd> / <Kbd>End</Kbd> jump.
- Disabled controls are skipped by arrows; inputs keep arrow keys for the caret.
